  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#937;</mi><mo>=</mo></math>sample space</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo></math>be an event</p><p>So,&nbsp;</p><p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#981;</mi></math></p><p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#937;</mi></math></p><p>Hence, both statements are true.</p>"
